From 8a1be81cd642701b6e7b4caaa7c01cba8934f584 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:53:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pvr: Don't regenerate the render setup for every dynamic
 render

With dynamic rendering, which Zink uses, every vkCmdBeginRendering set
up its render state from scratch: the load op programs, the SPM end of
tile program and new RT datasets (with their free lists) were compiled,
uploaded and created again for every render, and the end of tile
program for every job, whatever API was used.

Cache them in the device instead:
- the load op programs, by the clears/loads state and the render target
  resources they are generated from,
- the end of tile programs (per job and SPM), by their properties,
- the render targets, by render size, shared by all the dynamic renders
  of that size as the renders of a framebuffer share them.

Each cache is bounded; once full, things are set up per render as
before.

On a GE8300 (TrimUI Smart Pro), CPU use of one core at 60 fps:
weston-simple-egl on Zink 71% -> 22%, the cage compositor (Zink)
compositing vkcube 42% -> 14%, vkcube on VK_KHR_display 22% -> 12%.

Signed-off-by: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
